The first cut of the /spawn write tap is in as commit 3b7258e6 (Part of #1014). Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass.

What it does now: a foreground /spawn run takes a git status snapshot of the main checkout right before the worker starts and another right after it finishes. The second snapshot is taken before -o writes the output file you asked for. It then prints one line on stderr listing the paths that appear only in the second snapshot, showing up to 10 names:

⚠ write tap: N paths changed in the main checkout outside the worker's worktree while it ran: …

• When there are none, the line says 0 and adds "(only paths git sees are counted)", so a zero doesn't read as proof nothing was touched.
• When the snapshot can't be taken (not a git repo, or git fails), it prints "could not check" instead of 0.
• The tap is skipped when no worktree was created, because then the worker runs in your checkout on purpose.
• The worker's own tree under .yoyo/worktrees/ is the only thing excluded.
• Path names are cleaned of control characters before printing, and the line has no glyphs in plain-output mode.
• The new code is in src/spawn_write_tap.rs. It calls git through the existing src/git.rs helpers, as a repo test requires.

What it misses:
• Writes outside the repo (/tmp, $HOME, other repos) and gitignored files.
• A file that was already modified before the run and gets changed again, or one the run reverts.
• It reports what changed "while it ran", not what the worker wrote, so your own edits during the run are counted too.
• --bg and --parallel aren't wired. During a background run the parent session keeps editing the same checkout, so a before/after diff would mostly count the parent's own changes. That needs a different design and stays open on #1014.

Tests: 11 tests in the new module, including one on a real temporary repo where one new file gives exactly 1 path. Making outside_writes return nothing turned that test and the table test red by name. Restoring it turned all 11 green, and no NEUTERED marker is left.

`commands_spawn.rs` size cap: the file had no room left under its cap. I paid for the wiring by deleting its duplicate copies of run_git_in and repo_root, which now come from spawn_worktree.rs. The file went from 4576 to 4570 lines and I lowered its cap to match.

ARCHITECTURE.md has a new entry for the module, and docs/src/usage/commands.md has a short paragraph on the new line. I commented on #1014 with the commit and the lists above. Nothing goes to #734 yet: the promise there was the first number from a real worker run, and no real run has printed one.
